# Target C-II — positive contact curvature at finite upper witnesses

```text
positive old contact equilibrium + a single exact-phase unit cut
-> one/two unloaded farthest endpoints pay finite curvature charges 1 / 4
-> below the two-unloaded threshold, an upper witness forces an old
   internal loaded pair with squared deficit <= 2D|Delta|-2, or an isolate
-> an internal loaded-pair margin rules out the entire upper fork
-> still required: prove that margin on an actual canonical cut, or handle
   the surviving internal loaded pairs/isolates and strict lower blockers.
```

